#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415767 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415767 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415767 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9c4c4c60-58a2-5309-91fd-f009939a8cdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415770 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415770 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77250" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415770 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415770 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/87/87182d625f4e669a6b2791a17f3e12c34922043b8f3deefd6b2473e8fb529886.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a section of the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(0,4).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415770 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3412530f-81b3-51bb-95a9-4599a55eb207" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415770 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nLet ${C}_{2}$ be the section of parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ from $A$ to $B.$ Then,\n $-{C}_{2}$ will be the same path but travelled from $B$ to $A.$ The path $-{C}_{2}$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t)=t\\,i+(4-{t}^{2})\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<2.$ Along this curve, we have $x=t$ and $y=4-{t}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =x\\,i=t\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i-2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =(t\\,i)\\cdot (i-2t\\,j) \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =2-{\\int }_{0}^{2}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2-{\\int }_{0}^{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2-{[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2-[\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415772 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415772 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415772 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415772 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/74/746a05b2345e50173ed898b741944ba435d17a44dfc075848be9d8fcd2f2ad90.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $PQRP,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415772 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6da1b103-36df-5031-b2ef-46cb571416a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415772 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={-{C}_{1}}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ is the same path as ${C}_{1}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415775 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415775 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415775 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415775 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+{e}^{x}\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415775 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a47f5f1d-1328-52e8-8c90-bfca32946e28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415775 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186424625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1045 "Properties of Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186424625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424601 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "c1a363ff-d156-5c04-b913-8176faf9c905" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424602 #edb/ref 1080 "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424602 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175